   "tabId": null,
   "text": "My WPF clipboard application has a text-rendering quality issue. Text appears blurry, pixelated, or slightly distorted, but this happens ONLY inside my application.\r\n\r\nMy laptop display resolution is 1920×1200, and all other Windows applications render text perfectly.\r\n\r\nI want you to investigate and fix the root cause of the issue.\r\n\r\nPlease check the following areas:\r\n\r\nDPI Awareness\r\nVerify that the application is properly DPI-aware.\r\nCheck the application manifest for Per-Monitor DPI awareness (preferably PerMonitorV2).\r\nEnsure WPF is not being affected by incorrect DPI scaling.\r\nWPF Text Rendering\r\nCheck TextOptions.TextFormattingMode.\r\nCheck TextOptions.TextRenderingMode.\r\nCheck RenderOptions.BitmapScalingMode.\r\nEnsure text is rendered using appropriate ClearType or grayscale antialiasing settings.\r\nInvestigate whether any visual elements are being rendered as bitmaps instead of vector-based text.\r\nScaling and Layout\r\nCheck whether the main window or any parent containers use ScaleTransform or other scaling transformations.\r\nLook for fractional pixel positioning or layout rounding issues.\r\nEnable UseLayoutRounding and evaluate SnapsToDevicePixels where appropriate.\r\nWindows C",
